# CMMC L1 / NIST 800-171 3.5.1 - Identify users, processes, and devices
# Platform: M365 (Entra ID)
# Check type: m365_graph_query against /users

META
    esp_id `cmmc-l1-3-5-1-m365-identifier-management-001`
    version `1.0.0`
    dsl_schema_version `1.0.0`
    platform `m365`
    criticality `high`

    title `CMMC L1 IA.L1-3.5.1: Identify information system users`
    description `Validates that every directory account holds a unique, non-empty userPrincipalName, providing a stable identifier for authentication, authorization, and audit attribution.`
    author `scanset-security`
    tags `m365,cmmc-l1,nist-800-171,3-5-1,ia,identifier-management`

    control_mapping `NIST-800-171:3.5.1`
    control_objective `3.5.1`

    assessment_method `TEST`
    implementation_status `implemented`
    responsible_role `system-admin`

    control_origination `sp-system`
    inherited_from `M365:tenant:identity-baseline`
    customer_responsibility `configuration`

    remediation_days `7`
    recommendation `Audit /users to confirm every account holds a non-empty userPrincipalName. Investigate any account presenting without a UPN as it likely indicates a synchronization or provisioning fault.`

    component_id `comp-m365-identity`

    impl_3_5_1 `Information system users are identified by a unique userPrincipalName issued and managed by the identity provider. The userPrincipalName is the stable identifier referenced by authentication, authorization, role assignment, and audit subsystems, ensuring every action in the system is attributable to a specific named principal. Identifier uniqueness is enforced by the directory at provisioning time; reuse is prevented across the account lifecycle.`

META_END

DEF
    OBJECT all_users
        path `users`
    OBJECT_END

    STATE all_users_have_upn
        found boolean = true
        record
            field rows.*.userPrincipalName string contains `@`
            field rows.*.id string != ``
        record_end
    STATE_END

    CRI AND
        CTN m365_graph_query
            TEST all all AND
            STATE_REF all_users_have_upn
            OBJECT_REF all_users
        CTN_END
    CRI_END
DEF_END
